{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "milestone": {
        "id": "tnib-m001",
        "slug": "v1-mvp-launch",
        "path": "data/tnib-m001--v1-mvp-launch.md",
        "version": 2,
        "title": "v1.0 MVP Launch",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "type": "milestone",
        "priority": "critical",
        "created_at": "2026-02-15T09:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-25T14:30:00Z",
        "body": "\nShip the minimum viable product with core task management, user authentication, basic dashboard, and API foundation.\n\n## Goal\n\nDeliver a working product that early adopters can use for daily project management by end of Q1 2026.\n\n## Current Focus\n\n- Completing OAuth2 authentication flow\n- Stabilizing task management CRUD operations\n- Addressing critical security bugs before beta\n\n## Key Decisions\n\n- Chose PostgreSQL over MongoDB for ACID compliance requirements\n- REST API first, GraphQL deferred to v1.2\n- Server-side rendering deferred — SPA with Svelte for now\n",
        "documents": [
          "docs/product-roadmap.md"
        ],
        "order": "a",
        "etag": "a43cadc3b6d5eefc"
      },
      "progress": {
        "total": 4,
        "done": 0,
        "percent": 0,
        "scrapped": 0,
        "deferred": 0
      },
      "queue": [
        {
          "nib": {
            "id": "tnib-e001",
            "slug": "user-authentication",
            "path": "data/tnib-e001--user-authentication.md",
            "version": 2,
            "title": "User Authentication",
            "status": "in-progress",
            "type": "epic",
            "priority": "high",
            "created_at": "2026-02-18T10:00:00Z",
            "updated_at": "2026-03-24T16:00:00Z",
            "body": "\n## Objective\n\nImplement a complete authentication system supporting email/password, OAuth2 social providers, and secure session management.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Users can register and log in with email/password\n- [x] Passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost 12)\n- [ ] OAuth2 login via Google and GitHub\n- [ ] Password reset via email link\n- [ ] Sessions invalidated on password change\n\n## Scope Boundaries\n\n- MFA is out of scope for v1.0\n- SAML/SSO deferred to enterprise tier\n",
            "documents": [
              "docs/auth-architecture.md"
            ],
            "milestone": "tnib-m001",
            "milestone_order": "a",
            "etag": "087d0acaf343def5"
          },
          "progress": {
            "total": 6,
            "done": 1,
            "percent": 17,
            "scrapped": 0,
            "deferred": 0
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "tnib-f002",
              "slug": "oauth2-social-login",
              "path": "data/tnib-f002--oauth2-social-login.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "OAuth2 social login",
              "status": "in-progress",
              "type": "feature",
              "priority": "normal",
              "estimate": "l",
              "created_at": "2026-02-25T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-24T15:00:00Z",
              "body": "\nAllow users to log in via Google and GitHub OAuth2 providers. Account linking when email matches existing account.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Google OAuth2 login flow\n- [ ] GitHub OAuth2 login flow\n- [ ] Account linking for matching emails\n- [ ] Graceful handling of denied permissions\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e001",
              "order": "b",
              "area": "auth",
              "etag": "7fb15e73551a9f57"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-f003",
              "slug": "password-reset-flow",
              "path": "data/tnib-f003--password-reset-flow.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Password reset flow",
              "status": "todo",
              "type": "feature",
              "priority": "normal",
              "estimate": "m",
              "created_at": "2026-03-01T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "body": "\nEmail-based password reset with secure token generation and configurable expiry.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] \"Forgot password\" page sends reset email\n- [ ] Token valid for 1 hour, single-use\n- [ ] Rate limiting on reset requests\n- [ ] Password strength validation on new password\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e001",
              "order": "c",
              "etag": "e1525b2ef99f4327"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-t008",
              "slug": "auth-api-documentation",
              "path": "data/tnib-t008--auth-api-documentation.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Write authentication API documentation",
              "status": "draft",
              "type": "task",
              "priority": "low",
              "estimate": "m",
              "tags": [
                "docs"
              ],
              "created_at": "2026-03-10T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "body": "\n## Description\n\nDocument all authentication endpoints in the API reference: registration, login, logout, OAuth flows, password reset, and session management.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [ ] OpenAPI spec updated with auth endpoints\n- [ ] Request/response examples for each endpoint\n- [ ] Error code reference table\n- [ ] Authentication flow diagrams\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e001",
              "order": "d",
              "etag": "4eb881098a68bb98"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-b002",
              "slug": "session-tokens-not-invalidated",
              "path": "data/tnib-b002--session-tokens-not-invalidated.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Session tokens not invalidated on password change",
              "status": "todo",
              "type": "bug",
              "priority": "critical",
              "estimate": "m",
              "tags": [
                "security"
              ],
              "created_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-20T09:00:00Z",
              "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Log in on Device A\n2. Change password on Device A\n3. Check Device B — still logged in with old session\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** All other sessions invalidated after password change\n**Actual:** Existing sessions remain valid indefinitely\n\n## Root Cause\n\nPassword change handler updates the password hash but doesn't increment the session generation counter. The session validation middleware doesn't check generation — it only validates the session token exists in Redis.\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e001",
              "order": "e",
              "area": "auth",
              "etag": "0bc8a984518686e6"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-b001",
              "slug": "oauth-callback-url-mismatch",
              "path": "data/tnib-b001--oauth-callback-url-mismatch.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "OAuth callback URL mismatch in production config",
              "status": "todo",
              "type": "bug",
              "priority": "high",
              "estimate": "s",
              "created_at": "2026-03-18T14:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-22T09:00:00Z",
              "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Deploy to production environment\n2. Click \"Login with Google\"\n3. Complete Google consent screen\n4. Observe \"redirect_uri_mismatch\" error\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** User redirected back to app and logged in\n**Actual:** Google returns `redirect_uri_mismatch` error because production config still has staging callback URL\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL` environment variable in production is set to `https://staging.taskflow.dev/auth/callback` instead of `https://taskflow.dev/auth/callback`. Terraform config has the correct value but it wasn't applied after the last deploy.\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e001",
              "order": "f",
              "etag": "dcf001176210eb43"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nib": {
            "id": "tnib-e002",
            "slug": "task-management-core",
            "path": "data/tnib-e002--task-management-core.md",
            "version": 2,
            "title": "Task Management Core",
            "status": "in-progress",
            "type": "epic",
            "priority": "high",
            "created_at": "2026-02-18T10:30:00Z",
            "updated_at": "2026-03-25T09:00:00Z",
            "body": "\n## Objective\n\nBuild the core task CRUD, assignment, prioritization, and subtask systems that form the backbone of the product.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Full CRUD for tasks with validation\n- [x] Task assignment to users\n- [ ] Priority-based sorting and drag-and-drop reordering\n- [ ] Subtask/checklist support with depth limits\n\n## Scope Boundaries\n\n- Recurring tasks deferred to v1.2\n- Gantt chart view deferred to v1.1\n",
            "milestone": "tnib-m001",
            "milestone_order": "b",
            "etag": "6fcdd5030cc73bfb"
          },
          "progress": {
            "total": 7,
            "done": 1,
            "percent": 14,
            "scrapped": 0,
            "deferred": 0
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "tnib-f005",
              "slug": "task-assignment-and-ownership",
              "path": "data/tnib-f005--task-assignment-and-ownership.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Task assignment and ownership",
              "status": "in-progress",
              "type": "feature",
              "priority": "normal",
              "estimate": "m",
              "created_at": "2026-03-01T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-23T11:00:00Z",
              "body": "\nAssign tasks to team members with ownership tracking and notification on assignment changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Assign/unassign users to tasks\n- [x] User-task relationship model\n- [ ] Email notification on assignment\n- [ ] Bulk assignment via API\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e002",
              "order": "b",
              "etag": "9d8f2d4aa2605a63"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-f006",
              "slug": "task-prioritization-and-sorting",
              "path": "data/tnib-f006--task-prioritization-and-sorting.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Task prioritization and sorting",
              "status": "todo",
              "type": "feature",
              "priority": "normal",
              "estimate": "l",
              "created_at": "2026-03-05T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "body": "\nAllow users to prioritize tasks with drag-and-drop reordering and optional auto-sorting by priority level.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Drag-and-drop reordering within a list\n- [ ] Priority-based auto-sort toggle\n- [ ] Persisted custom order per user per board\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e002",
              "order": "c",
              "etag": "da4d32ac8d8f8309"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-f007",
              "slug": "subtask-and-checklist-support",
              "path": "data/tnib-f007--subtask-and-checklist-support.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Subtask and checklist support",
              "status": "draft",
              "type": "feature",
              "priority": "low",
              "estimate": "xl",
              "created_at": "2026-03-10T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "body": "\nSupport nested subtasks and checklists within tasks, with progress aggregation and configurable depth limits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Create subtasks nested under a parent task\n- [ ] Checklist items with completion toggle\n- [ ] Progress percentage aggregated from subtask completion\n- [ ] Configurable max nesting depth (default: 3)\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e002",
              "order": "d",
              "etag": "ab249c781e46d1c2"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-t018",
              "slug": "performance-benchmark-10k",
              "path": "data/tnib-t018--performance-benchmark-10k.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Performance benchmark for 10k tasks",
              "status": "todo",
              "type": "task",
              "priority": "normal",
              "estimate": "m",
              "tags": [
                "perf"
              ],
              "created_at": "2026-03-10T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "body": "\n## Description\n\nLoad test with 10,000 tasks to establish baseline performance metrics. Identify bottlenecks in list rendering and API response times.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [ ] Seed script creates 10k tasks with realistic data\n- [ ] API list endpoint responds in \u003c200ms at p95\n- [ ] UI list renders without jank (60fps scroll)\n- [ ] Document baseline metrics for future regression checks\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e002",
              "order": "e",
              "etag": "71ec204e7cd544ab"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-b004",
              "slug": "task-title-truncation",
              "path": "data/tnib-b004--task-title-truncation.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Task title silently truncated at 255 characters",
              "status": "todo",
              "type": "bug",
              "priority": "low",
              "estimate": "s",
              "created_at": "2026-03-12T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
              "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create a task with a title longer than 255 characters via API\n2. Read the task back\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Either accept full title (up to our stated 500 char limit) or return 400 if too long\n**Actual:** Title silently truncated to 255 chars by database column constraint\n\n## Root Cause\n\nDatabase column is `VARCHAR(255)` but API validation allows up to 500 chars. Either widen the column to 500 or lower the API limit to 255.\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e002",
              "order": "f",
              "etag": "2543a9599e9427fe"
            },
            {
              "id": "tnib-b003",
              "slug": "deactivated-user-assignment",
              "path": "data/tnib-b003--deactivated-user-assignment.md",
              "version": 2,
              "title": "Assigning task to deactivated user shows no error",
              "status": "in-progress",
              "type": "bug",
              "priority": "high",
              "estimate": "s",
              "created_at": "2026-03-20T09:00:00Z",
              "updated_at": "2026-03-24T15:00:00Z",
              "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Deactivate user \"alice@example.com\" via admin panel\n2. Assign a task to \"alice@example.com\" via API\n3. Request succeeds with 200 OK\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** 400 Bad Request with message \"Cannot assign to deactivated user\"\n**Actual:** Assignment succeeds silently; task shows as assigned to a ghost user\n\n## Root Cause\n\nAssignment endpoint only checks if user ID exists in users table, doesn't check `is_active` flag. Need to add `WHERE is_active = true` to the user lookup query.\n",
              "parent": "tnib-e002",
              "order": "g",
              "etag": "032d374cfa51e23c"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nib": {
            "id": "tnib-e003",
            "slug": "dashboard-and-reporting",
            "path": "data/tnib-e003--dashboard-and-reporting.md",
            "version": 2,
            "title": "Dashboard \u0026 Reporting",
            "status": "todo",
            "type": "epic",
            "priority": "normal",
            "created_at": "2026-02-20T11:00:00Z",
            "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:00:00Z",
            "body": "\n## Objective\n\nProvide team leads with velocity charts, personal dashboards, and exportable reports.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Team velocity chart with sprint-over-sprint comparison\n- [ ] Personal \"My Tasks\" dashboard with widget layout\n- [ ] Export to CSV and PDF\n\n## Scope Boundaries\n\n- Custom report builder deferred to v1.2\n- Real-time dashboard updates require v1.1 WebSocket infrastructure\n",
            "blocked_by": [
              "tnib-e002"
            ],
            "milestone": "tnib-m001",
            "milestone_order": "c",
            "etag": "d05893dc1ec8fb30"
          },
